Subject: [PATCH] Windows: do not match the JIT guard page on a thread that has none

ResetToConsistentState() consults JITGuardPage::HandleJITGuardPage() for every EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION,
before it has decided whether the fault is in FEX code at all. The per-thread guard page is only
assigned by the JIT when the thread compiles its first block (JIT.cpp, Arm64JITCore::CompileCode), so
on a thread that has never run x64 code InternalThreadState::JITGuardPage is still 0, and the test

    Address >= JITGuardPage && Address < JITGuardPage + FEX_PAGE_SIZE

degenerates to "Address < 4096": every null-page dereference matches. FEX then loads the thread's
RestartJump buffer, which SetJump() has never filled, into the native context and NtContinue()s with
pc = sp = 0, so the process dies with a bare SIGSEGV on wine's unix side instead of the fault ever
reaching KiUserExceptionDispatcher.

Any native EC code that faults on the null page from a thread that has never JIT-compiled is affected.
An ARM64EC build of the Mono runtime hits it on every managed NullReferenceException, which it
implements as a hardware fault near address 0 on threads that are native from their first instruction
(docs/research/mono-arm64ec.md).

Require an assigned guard page before matching.
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/JITGuardPage.h
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/JITGuardPage.h
@@ -5,7 +5,10 @@
 
 namespace FEX::Windows::JITGuardPage {
 static inline bool HandleJITGuardPage(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, void* Address, uint64_t* GPRs, __uint128_t* FPRs, uint64_t* PC) {
-  if (Address >= reinterpret_cast<void*>(Thread->JITGuardPage) &&
+  // A thread that has never compiled a block has no guard page yet (JITGuardPage == 0). Without this check a
+  // fault anywhere in the null page (e.g. a native null dereference at address 0x10) would match the window
+  // [0, FEX_PAGE_SIZE) and "resume" through the never-initialised RestartJump buffer, i.e. at pc = sp = 0.
+  if (Thread->JITGuardPage && Address >= reinterpret_cast<void*>(Thread->JITGuardPage) &&
       Address < reinterpret_cast<void*>(Thread->JITGuardPage + FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE)) {
     FEXCore::UncheckedLongJump::ManuallyLoadJumpBuf(Thread->RestartJump, Thread->JITGuardOverflowArgument, GPRs, FPRs, PC);
     return true;
